  if(preset==='desk')html=`<span class="badge">DESIGNED REFERENCE OBJECTS</span><h2>Ordinary objects.<br>Nested parts.</h2><p>A desktop, notebook, mug and two pens occupy one centimeter reference space. Select the blue pen to inspect its components.</p><button class="enter" data-enter="pen:blue">Enter the pen →</button><p class="limit">Dimensions and construction are chosen for this practice scene. This is not a scanned desk or a calibrated material simulation.</p>`;
  if(preset==='anatomy')html=`<span class="badge warm">ILLUSTRATIVE ANATOMY STUDY</span><h2>From tissue<br>to a cell.</h2><p>A schematic sheet of cells gives you an intermediate scale between everyday objects and molecules. Enter a cell to explore its illustrative internal parts.</p><button class="enter" data-enter="cell:cell">Enter a cell →</button><p class="limit">Generic designed forms; no measured tissue geometry, human specimen or cell-type-specific reconstruction. The 3D layout is a navigation exercise.</p>`;
